title mul-a seats and the taste of runes -- the composed cond parses on the 338a precedent, and the custodian answers three style questions
prompt Keaton's word approved the recommendations; the mul ruling landed as mul-a by the house's own STOA338a precedent (parse seats, lower waits), and mid-lap he asked the custodian's questions: is the shorthand good for Glow, would comlink-tendency naming defeat its artistic TAME purpose, and :: versus // for comments.
think mul-a, the mechanism: rune_shop_gate.rye's GateSpec gains face3 with its slice helper; the bracket header admits an optional third face (distinct from both siblings, nested @u32); parse_body's cond path learns exactly one composed form -- (gth face (mul face2 face3)) with literal decimal arms, gth alone in v1 -- seating BodyKind .cond_gth_mul; the tail-validation switch requires all three faces for the mul body, refuses a dangling third face on a pair body, and MulNotYetLowered joins the parse error set beside its 338a sibling; lower_shop_gate.rye answers it at eleven switch arms until mul-b emits. Proven: five new witness legs GREEN (the parse to the right spec, three refusals by name, the lower's honest wait) beside all 114 elder greens; the first attempt died at the tail switch whose else refused any face2 -- the validation the elder wrote caught the newcomer exactly as designed. TAME clean; width clean.
think The custodian's answers, held as recommendations for his word. THE SHORTHAND: yes, at the skeleton -- the runes are a closed learnable table that mark Glow's high register visually, and the desks' own practice already carries the newcomer with plain-word :: headers (name, shape, invariant, example) before a single rune, the mechanism-before-metaphor law wearing language clothes. THE COMLINK TENDENCY: it does not defeat the purpose because it governs a different layer -- everything Glow NAMES (desks, faces, shapes) already takes the clearest warm word (width, height, lit, gate-skate-kind-ceiling), while the operator table (gth, eq, mul) stays a closed inherited set where consistency beats piecemeal warmth; renaming operators one at a time would break the table property that makes the set learnable in an afternoon. COMMENTS: keep :: -- it marks the register at a glance where // would blur Glow into Rye at the seam the two-room family wants visible, the double colon reads as a manuscript margin, 428 living .glow files already speak it, and it is the ancestor's mark kept as gratitude made visible; the honest counterpoint (// lowers first-second friction) is answered by the header CONTENT carrying the newcomer, not the glyph.
obs mul-b -- the emit, with overflow refused by name in the lowered Rye -- is the booked sibling, exactly as 338b followed 338a. The claims law lit <= width x height becomes sayable the day it lands.
loom mul_a=parsed legs=5 elder_greens=114 switch_arms=11 tame=clean width=clean
